title Caravan ladder fold K -- the plainest fold, and the carry that was not spent
prompt Pick up the running thread, close open agent-closable reds first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; read one council-rota doc; sweep the prose Radiant; send.
think Standfast first. REDS reads 102 rows and every one closed, %101 and %102 released last lap, so no red books this allocation and the constructive queue opens honestly.
think Council rota by lap index. The index holds 1,481 rows, and 1481 mod 27 + 1 lands on item 24, the grain and the crossing. Its sameness strand reads straight onto this lap -- one value model, one fold, one vocabulary, and count the whole cost of a line saved. A fold that trades 457 lines of body for 157 of harness and call is that strand paying out.
think The card sized the next crux as tell_desist_runs, eight rungs at fifty lines apiece, all eight collapsing to one hash under the pair-and-depth mask. Measured rather than trusted, and it came out simpler than the card claimed -- the nesting depth is identical across all eight, so only the pair of words varies. Fold H's shape with nothing added at all.
think Verification before the edit, as every fold in this arc has done. Nine symbols wanted widening by one word across the eight -- abandoning_of, recanting_of, amending_of, couriering_of, disputing_of, abiding_of, lapsing_of, reposing_of, appeal_of -- with below_of a tenth in the desisting rung alone. max_queue_len already stood pub in all eight, so the harness reads the bound through the type handed in.
think The harness ends by calling its own sibling tell_desist_half rather than the rung's private delegate, since every rung's delegate is a pure forward with the same two words. That widens nothing and keeps the chain inside ladder_checks.rye.
think Parity proven by running rather than argued. All eight rungs built and run before the edit and after, every sorted multiset identical with zero lines differing, and the ordered diffs of four to sixteen lines each a concurrent-client line standing in the same count on both sides.
think The control folds I and J established settled the interleave again -- an unchanged binary run twice against itself differs by fourteen ordered lines with zero sorted difference, the same shape and a larger magnitude than the fold's own diff.
obs The one raw reach remaining is named in the harness rather than hidden. The absorbed tally sits four levels below abandoning_of because no rung publishes an accessor reaching that tier. The chain stood at the same depth in all eight, so it lifts literally and now stands once, where a single reading governs every rung that calls in. Fold J's lesson says name it; the comment says exactly that, and an accessor born for that tier is the next lap's cheap work.
obs The two rows a lift could most easily have inflated stood still for the seventh fold running -- the byte-identical check carry at 47 and the orchestration spine at 0. A cost removed rather than traded, seven laps in a row.
obs The neighbor walk's gap narrowed 21 percent to 13, by the same mechanism that widened it two laps ago. The walk orders rungs by file length, so a fold shrinking eight rungs by forty-nine lines apiece moves its own pairing. Widening and narrowing stay one property seen twice.
obs The finding that outweighs the fold. Six folds all lived inside the tell_ family, and the arc's record had drifted into reading the staircase is spent as a claim about the whole ladder. Asking the masked question of every printing body rather than the tell_ ones alone disagrees: stand_taking_and_returning_reach carries 1,435 lines across 42 of its 44 rungs at one hash, larger than any single fold this arc has taken, and run_dependent carries 1,386 across 43 of 67. Neither had ever been looked at.
obs I wrote the spent claim into caravan/README.md myself this lap and corrected it in the same lap once the wider meter answered. That is the REDS %102 family once more in its gentlest form -- a guard, or a narrative, that reads a subset in the voice of the whole. Measurement beats memory, including the memory written down six laps running.
